**Describe the bug**
When using the load() function in _layout.svelte and index.svelte, the returned data of index gets overridden by _layout. 
The index props load once with the right data (I can see the page). Afterwards `export let data` gets overridden.

**Logs**
![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/13353525/117114025-982bd180-ad8b-11eb-9a89-59638de9e366.png)

**To Reproduce**
Create similiar files an run the dev server:

index.svelte
```js
<script context="module">
  export async function load({ page, fetch }) {
    const query = ` some gql `;
    const response = await fetch("http://localhost:1337/graphql", {
      method: "POST",
      headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
      body: JSON.stringify({
        query,
      }),
    });
    const json = await response.json();
    console.log("index: ", json);    // layout data

    return {
      props: {
        data: json,
      },
    };
  }
</script>

<script>
  export let data;
</script>
```

_layout.svelte
```js
<script context="module">
  export async function load({ page, fetch }) {
    const query = ` some other gql `;
    const response = await fetch("http://localhost:1337/graphql", {
      method: "POST",
      headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
      body: JSON.stringify({
        query,
      }),
    });
    const json = await response.json();
    console.log("json: ", json);

    return {
      props: {
        data: json,
      },
    };
  }
</script>

<script>
  export let data;

  $: console.log("index:  ", data);  // undefined
</script>
```

**Expected behavior**
Load in index.svelte should query right data and props should not be overridden.

